.\"  -*- nroff -*-
.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt MCD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mcd.conf
.Nd mcd configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr mcd 8
reads
.Nm
at start and on
.Dv SIGHUP .
Without it, or without any
.Cm iface
line,
.Nm mcd
is passive on all interfaces.
.Pp
Each line holds global settings or one
.Cm iface
directive with its flags.  Comments start with
.Dq #
and run to the end of line.
.Sh GLOBAL SETTINGS
These apply to both IGMP and MLD, and to all interfaces.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm global-query-interval Ar SEC
Seconds between General Queries when elected querier, 1 to 1024,
default 125.  Values below 10 are not recommended.
.It Cm global-response-interval Ar SEC
Maximum response time hosts get for a General Query, 1 to 1024,
default 10.  A longer time spreads the reports out.
.It Cm global-last-member-interval Ar SEC
Seconds between the group specific queries sent after a leave, 1 to
1024, default 1.  The number of such queries is the
.Cm robustness .
.It Cm robustness Ar NUM
Tolerance to lost packets, 2 to 10, default 2.  Also the number of
queries in the startup burst.
.It Cm router-timeout Ar SEC
Time to wait for a silent querier before taking over, the other
querier present interval, 1 to 1024.  When unset it is calculated per
RFC 3376:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
robustness * query-interval + response-interval / 2
.Ed
.Pp
Set it only to interoperate with devices that do not follow the RFC.
.It Cm router-alert on | off , no router-alert
IP Router Alert option in IGMP queries, on by default for stacks that
hard-code the IP header length.  MLD queries always carry the IPv6
Router Alert option.
.It Cm topology-query on | off , no topology-query
General query when a port of the bridge starts forwarding, on by
default.  Link up, STP settling and a port added to the bridge all
count.  Hosts behind the port are back in the MDB within the response
interval instead of at the next periodic query, RFC 4541 \(sc2.1.1.
Sent only while
.Nm mcd
is the querier, at most one per second per interface, followed by the
startup burst.  Applies to the bridge itself and to VLAN interfaces on
top of it.
.It Cm mrd-interval Ar SEC
Multicast Router Discovery advertisement interval, 4 to 180, default
20.  For interfaces with
.Cm mrd on ,
see below.
.It Cm include Ar PATH
Read another file, or every file matching a
.Xr glob 3
pattern, e.g.\&
.Pa /etc/mc.d/*.conf .
.El
.Sh INTERFACES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm iface Ar IFNAME Op Ar FLAG ...
Configure the queriers of an interface, the bridge itself or a VLAN
interface on top of it.  The interface does not need to exist yet,
.Nm mcd
picks it up when it appears.  The keyword
.Cm phyint
is an alias.
.El
.Pp
The flags are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm enable | disable
Run the queriers on the interface, or not.  Default
.Cm disable .
.It Cm igmp on | off , mld on | off
Run the IGMP or the MLD querier, both on by default.
.It Cm igmpv1 | igmpv2 | igmpv3
IGMP version to start with, default
.Cm igmpv3 .
.Nm mcd
falls back to older versions on its own when such hosts are heard.
.It Cm mldv1 | mldv2
MLD version to start with, default
.Cm mldv2 ,
with the same fallback.
.It Cm mrd on | off
Multicast Router Discovery, RFC 4286, off by default.  Advertises
.Nm mcd
as a multicast router to the snooping switches on the LAN, so they
forward membership reports, and all multicast, towards it.  For
switches that learn their router ports from MRD rather than from
queries.  Three advertisements go out shortly after the interface comes
up, then one every
.Cm mrd-interval
seconds, and one in answer to a solicitation.  A
termination is sent when the interface goes down or
.Nm mcd
exits.  An interface in proxy mode has no address to advertise and
sends nothing.
.It Cm proxy-mode
Send proxy queries, from 0.0.0.0 or ::, which never win an election.
This makes
.Nm mcd
a backup querier on LANs that have a multicast router.  An interface
without an address is always in proxy mode.  The old name
.Cm proxy-queries
is accepted too.
.It Cm query-interval Ar SEC
Per interface override of
.Cm global-query-interval .
.It Cm static-group Ar GROUP
Join an IPv4 or IPv6 group on the interface, can be given more than
once.  The kernel then answers queries for the group like any host, so
a bridge keeps a permanent host membership for it in the MDB and always
forwards it to itself.  The membership stays until the group is
removed from the configuration or
.Nm mcd
exits, a link flap or a reload does not touch it.  Not supported in
raw VLAN mode.
.It Cm vlan Ar VID
Raw VLAN mode on a VLAN filtering bridge, 1 to 4094.  The querier runs
on that VLAN of the bridge without a VLAN interface on top, by injecting
tagged frames.  It is always in proxy mode.  Give
.Cm vlan
more than once to run a querier on several VLANs.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/mcd.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/mcd.conf
Default location, follows the identity set with
.Fl i ,
see
.Xr mcd 8 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Queriers on two VLAN interfaces, the second starting out in IGMPv2 and
MLDv1:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
iface vlan1 enable
iface vlan2 enable igmpv2 mldv1
.Ed
.Pp
IGMP only, with a shorter query interval:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
iface br0 enable mld off query-interval 30
.Ed
.Pp
A backup querier, and a querier on VLAN 42 of a filtering bridge:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
iface vlan3 enable proxy-mode
iface br0 vlan 42 enable
.Ed
.Pp
Static groups, and per interface snippets in a directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
iface vlan1 enable static-group 239.1.1.1 static-group ff05::1
include /etc/mc.d/*.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mcd 8 ,
.Xr mctl 8
.Sh AUTHORS
